WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.177
This example trims the email, removes characters outside a teaching-level allowed set,

00:00:05.177 --> 00:00:07.702
and converts the result to lowercase.

00:00:07.702 --> 00:00:11.447
Run it and compare original and cleaned values.

00:00:11.447 --> 00:00:15.777
Notice that cleaning a string does not prove the result is valid.

00:00:15.777 --> 00:00:19.252
Transformation and validation are separate steps.

00:00:19.252 --> 00:00:22.462
That distinction is important in data preparation.

00:00:22.462 --> 00:00:26.997
String functions are most useful when the text has a predictable structure.

00:00:26.997 --> 00:00:32.627
Before extracting a substring, confirm the delimiter or pattern really exists.

00:00:32.627 --> 00:00:38.417
Regular expressions are powerful, but a complicated regex can become hard to maintain;

00:00:38.417 --> 00:00:42.583
use the simplest rule that reliably matches the data you actually have.
